The rows above take effect when you restart Corbanu Terminal (you can restart
right after saving); until then this window's session keeps its current
settings, apart from Core's level and approval for every command (below). Your
config.toml is not modified.
Core's level is saved as Aggressive as soon as you confirm: agent commands
cannot run `corbanu vault …` and cannot open protected paths (the vault
store, sign-in files, credential files in your home folder such as .ssh, .aws
and .netrc, and Corbanu's config, history and state), sensitive surfaces need
a grant, external content reaches the model labelled untrusted, and memory
summaries stop. This window's session has not started yet: when it starts
here, it takes Core's level and approval for every command, and so do the other
sessions you start here before you restart. The other sessions of this Corbanu
Terminal running on this Corbanu home take it as soon as you confirm, with
approval for every command from their next turn.
Other Corbanu Terminals running on this Corbanu home take Core's Aggressive
protections and approval for every command within about a second of confirming,
and each says so; the rest of Aggressive starts there when they restart.
